# fleet.env.example — the site file for a four-node DGX Spark fleet. Copy it to launch/fleet.env (git-ignored) and
# replace every value: the values here are EXAMPLES, not defaults. Plain bash, sourced by every script in launch/
# and by bench/ar_bench.sh, bench/measure.sh and bench/stall_evidence.sh; keep the arrays as arrays, in rank order. Rank 0 is the node you run
# the scripts from; ranks 1-3 are reached with key-based ssh as USERS[r]@NODES[r].
# MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Aiden Le.

# NODES: the fabric (RoCE) IPv4 address of each rank, rank 0 first. This is the address NCCL, the RDMA runtime and
# the launcher's ssh use. Find it with `ip -br addr` on each node: the address on the interface that carries the RoCE
# subnet (a 200G ConnectX-7 port), not the management network.
NODES=(192.0.2.11 192.0.2.12 192.0.2.13 192.0.2.14)

# USERS: the login user on each rank, in the same order. Rank 0's entry is the local user; the others must accept
# `ssh USERS[r]@NODES[r]` from rank 0 without a password (ssh-copy-id) and be in the docker group there.
USERS=(alice alice bob bob)

# HOMES: the home directory of that user on each rank (`echo $HOME` there). The launcher looks for the checkpoint
# under it (INKLING_REPO_REL below) and creates two directories in it: inkling2-patches (the hooks of patches/ and,
# when their switches are on, the forked GEMM's module and the confidence head's file, copied at every launch) and
# inkling2-cache (JIT-compiled kernels, mounted as /root/.cache: the first boot compiles for
# about 17 minutes, later boots reuse it and take about 5).
HOMES=(/home/alice /home/alice /home/bob /home/bob)

# FABRIC_IFACE: the network interface that carries the NODES address, the same name on every node. From
# `ip -br addr`: the interface listed next to the fabric IPv4. NCCL and gloo bind their control sockets to it.
FABRIC_IFACE=enp1s0f0np0

# RDMA_HCAS: the RDMA devices to use, comma-separated, the same names on every node. `ls /sys/class/infiniband` lists
# them; list every function that faces the fabric (two per node on a Spark with both ConnectX-7 ports cabled). The
# launcher probes the FIRST one for the RoCE-v2 GID index of the NODES address on each node and passes it to NCCL and
# the RDMA runtime; a wrong index fails every RDMA connect, which is why it is probed and never assumed.
RDMA_HCAS=rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0

# FABRIC_SUBNET: the fabric subnet in CIDR form (from `ip -br addr`: the fabric address with its prefix length,
# e.g. 192.0.2.1/24 -> 192.0.2.0/24). NCCL restricts its RDMA addresses to it (NCCL_IB_ADDR_RANGE).
FABRIC_SUBNET=192.0.2.0/24

# LOG_DIR: where relaunch-inkling2.sh and the watchdog write their logs, the boot memory samples and the watchdog's
# postmortem captures, on rank 0. Relative to $HOME or absolute.
LOG_DIR=inkling2-logs

# SERVED_ALIASES: extra model ids to list on /v1/models and the Ollama-style /api/tags besides the served name
# inkling-2-small, comma-separated (for clients that ask for a fixed or a generic name). Empty by default. The form
# below lets an exported SERVED_ALIASES in the environment win over this file.
SERVED_ALIASES="${SERVED_ALIASES:-}"

# Optional: INKLING_IMAGE overrides the image (default lmsysorg/sglang:dev-inkling-2-small). The hooks were written
# against one build of that tag; the README gives its digest. If the tag has moved and a boot fails in the hooks,
# pin the digest here. The image must be pulled on every node.
#INKLING_IMAGE=lmsysorg/sglang@sha256:424c1da97f6d6eef1612006c77b2ca791657a8184c1fbdbc682ebf9485d3b32c

# Optional: where the checkpoint is on each node, relative to that rank's HOMES entry (default: the HuggingFace cache
# of that user), and the revision to serve (`ls <repo>/snapshots`). The launcher mounts the repo directory, not the
# snapshot inside it, so the snapshot's blob symlinks resolve.
#INKLING_REPO_REL=.cache/huggingface/hub/models--thinkingmachines--Inkling-2-Small
#INKLING_SNAP=snapshots/b0e7afb8892a07897c78ce1c5b801a0d9cbd5e7b

# Optional: OTHER_CONTAINER is the container name of another engine that may run on these nodes. While it runs on
# any rank the launcher's preflight aborts instead of starting next to it (both would want nearly all memory).
# Leave unset when this stack is the only one.
#OTHER_CONTAINER=
